From 319bab05f7fa3466ec405f00f888789846d95691 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-um-darwin patch replay <noreply@linux-um-darwin.invalid>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 23:44:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/39] uml: use one scalable Darwin native address profile

All Apple products should exercise one sparse software guest address contract
instead of allowing macOS to hide bugs behind a different kernel image or
virtual-address model. Remove the build-time standard/iOS split and give
macOS, Simulator, and device one 128 TiB software guest task range with a
scalable native hole.

Size the direct map from configured guest memory and retain a page-rounded
one-eighth auxiliary allowance with a 32 MiB floor. Apply that same limit to
UML vmalloc, and reject mmap, uaccess, and fault ranges which intersect the
active native hole rather than shrinking guest userspace around it.

Keep the shared ET_DYN kernel linked at 48 GiB. The host places it in the
physical-iOS window below 62 GiB on device and Simulator, or in macOS's high
native window. Derive the hole endpoint and kernel host-task ceiling from the
actual relocated image base so the same kernel bytes support both placements.

Make the signal-return trampoline follow the common task ceiling and carry
that constant through the versioned Darwin ABI.
